                <pb facs="0566" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11483.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé O’Shaughnessy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-10T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>740. You have received from Mayo, Vera Cruz, copy of message sent to local
                    Mexican general. The President directs that you present the matter at once to
                    the Foreign Office with utmost firmness, earnestness, and frankness,
                    representing to them the extreme seriousness of the situation and the
                    possibility that the gravest consequences may ensue unless the guilty parties
                    are promptly punished. Inform us of reply made and action taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
